//? Title: Compress a dense layer with truncated SVD
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

\abstract(
Approximate a nearly rank-three weight matrix and measure how the
retained rank changes storage and held-out prediction error.
)
\toc

Write the dense weights as \(W=U\operatorname{diag}(s)V^\top\), with
singular values in descending order. Keep the first \(r\) directions
and fold their singular values into the left factor. The compressed
prediction then uses two matrix products, \((XA)B\). The squared
Frobenius error of the weight approximation equals the sum of squared
omitted singular values. Output MSE also depends on how the input rows
project onto the omitted directions.

The simulated layer is a rank-three product plus Gaussian weight noise.
A separate set of 64 rows measures output error. The dense matrix has
120 weights, and the factors use \(22r\) weights. Rank five nearly
eliminates the output error but saves only ten weights.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/low_rank_factorization.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <random>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::mt19937 rng(11921);
  std::normal_distribution<double> normal;
  auto draw = [&](int rows, int columns) {
    std::vector<double> values(rows * columns);
    for (auto& value : values) value = normal(rng);
    return n::from_vector(values, {rows, columns});
  };
  const auto left = draw(12, 3);
  const auto right = draw(3, 10);
  const auto noise = draw(12, 10);
  const auto input = draw(64, 12);
  const auto dense = n::matmul(left, right) + .035 * noise;
  const auto full_output = n::matmul(input, dense);

  n::NamedTensors archive{{"input", input}, {"dense", dense}, {"dense_output", full_output}};
  std::vector<double> counts, log_errors;
  std::println("| Rank | Stored weights | Discarded energy | Held-out MSE |");
  std::println("| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |");
  for (int rank : {1, 2, 3, 5}) {
    const auto factors = n::factor_dense_weights(dense, rank);
    const auto prediction = factors.predict(input);
    const double mse = n::mse(prediction, full_output).item();
    const auto diff = dense - n::matmul(factors.left, factors.right);
    const double energy = n::sum(diff * diff).item();
    if (std::abs(energy - factors.discarded_energy) > 1e-10 || !(mse > 0))
      throw std::runtime_error("Truncated SVD energy or prediction check failed");
    if (rank == 1) archive.emplace_back("singular", factors.singular_values);
    const auto suffix = std::to_string(rank);
    archive.emplace_back("left_" + suffix, factors.left);
    archive.emplace_back("right_" + suffix, factors.right);
    archive.emplace_back("output_" + suffix, prediction);
    counts.push_back(factors.left.numel() + factors.right.numel());
    log_errors.push_back(std::log10(mse));
    std::println("| {} | {:.0f} / 120 | {:.8g} | {:.8g} |", rank, counts.back(), energy, mse);
  }

  const std::string directory = "build/low_rank_factorization/";
  std::filesystem::create_directories(directory);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::save_npz(directory + "factors.npz", archive);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(counts, log_errors, "Truncated SVD", {37, 99, 235})
      .points(counts, log_errors, "Ranks 1, 2, 3, 5", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .title("Held-out prediction error at four storage budgets")
      .x_label("Stored weights (full layer: 120)").y_label("log10 output MSE")
      .save_svg(directory + "tradeoff.svg");
  std::filesystem::copy_file(directory + "tradeoff.svg", "figures/low_rank_factorization.svg",
                             std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Rank | Stored weights | Discarded energy | Held-out MSE |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 22 / 120 | 127.92417 | 15.784215 |
| 2 | 44 / 120 | 53.123355 | 6.4584942 |
| 3 | 66 / 120 | 0.070023333 | 0.0070499834 |
| 5 | 110 / 120 | 0.023972053 | 0.0027801927 |
\image(figures/low_rank_factorization.svg)
// result_end

The largest drop in prediction error occurs when the third singular
direction is retained. Additional directions model some of the weight
noise and have a smaller effect.

> Reference

- [Eckart and Young, The approximation of one matrix by another of lower rank|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02288367].
